title: topic_player_monologue_statement
tags: actor:Prince
---
Prince: Man... where do I even start.

Prince: Name’s Prince. 
Prince: Yeah, for real. 
Prince: Ain’t no nickname, ain’t no joke. 
Prince: My momma actually named me that.
Prince: Guess she thought I’d grow up to be somebody special.

Prince: But nah. 
Prince: I grew up on the cold side of the city. 
Prince: The side where walls talk back, and the streets don’t ever sleep.

Prince: I learned quick that nobody’s gonna feed you unless you take the plate yourself.
Prince: So I took it.

Prince: They call us the Alley Cats. 
Prince: Twenty kids with nothin’ but hunger in their bellies and scars on their knees.
Prince: And I’m the one they look at when the world starts swingin’.

Prince: I ain’t their dad, but sometimes I wish I was.
Prince: I wish I could give ‘em what I never got.

Prince: Warm bed.
Prince: Full plate.
Prince: No cops.
Prince: No fear.
Prince: Just... peace, man.

Prince: That’s all I ever wanted.
Prince: For them to live good.
Prince: For them to make it out the alleys without endin’ up in cuffs or graves.

Prince: But see... that’s the funny part.
Prince: I got no clue how to do that.

Prince: All I ever knew was hustle, steal, survive.
Prince: One night at a time.
Prince: One breath at a time.

Prince: And now?
Prince: Now my own heart’s turnin’ against me.
Prince: Doctors say I got two years, maybe less.

Prince: Two years.
Prince: That’s all the time I got to fix somethin’ I don’t even know how to fix.

Prince: Every time I close my eyes, I see them...
Prince: My boys
Prince: Laughin’, 
Prince: Fightin’, 
Prince: Starvin’, 
Prince: Dreamin’.
Prince: And I ask myself
Prince: What happens when I’m gone?

Prince: Who’s gonna lead ‘em?
Prince: Who’s gonna keep ‘em safe?

Prince: My best friend Oldboy’s gone.
Prince: His brother too.
Prince: They left, man. Took my heart with ‘em.

Prince: Now it’s just me.
Prince: Me and twenty hungry mouths lookin’ up
Prince: Waitin’ for answers I don’t got.

Prince: ...

Prince: I’m scared, bro.
Prince: Not of dyin’.
Prince: I already made peace with that.

Prince: I’m scared of leavin’ them behind in the same dirt I found ‘em in.

Prince: Scared that all this...
Prince: the sleepless nights
Prince: the blood, the fights
Prince: meant nothin’.

Prince: ...

Prince: When you don’t know what to do…
Prince: You ask for help, right?

Prince: I met this old man at the hospital.
Prince: Like, same ward.
Prince: Name was Mister Hariri.

Prince: Sounded familiar, right?
Prince: Like I heard that name before.
Prince: And then it hit me—
Prince: Hariri Foundation.

Prince: Yeah, *that* Hariri.
Prince: Them big food companies in them clean stores.
Prince: The kinda places we never rob.
Prince: Too nice.
Prince: Too clean.
Prince: Too far from our world.

Prince: Anyway… this old man, he ain’t act like the rest.
Prince: Didn’t look down on me.
Prince: Didn’t flinch when he saw the jacket, the scars.
Prince: He just… looked at me.
Prince: Like he actually saw me.

Prince: I don’t know what he saw
Prince: maybe a kid who lost his way
Prince: maybe a fool who tried to play king
Prince: but he looked at me like I was still human.

Prince: So I told him straight.
Prince: Told him I’m tired.
Prince: Told him I don’t know what to do no more.
Prince: That everything I touch turns to dust.

**Prince:**
And he listened.
Didn’t interrupt.
Didn’t judge.
Just listened.

Prince: Then he said,
Prince: “You should visit the masjid, my son.
Prince: Find a man named Munir.
Prince: He will guide you.”

Prince: Masjid…
Prince: that’s a mosque, right?
Prince: Place where Muslims pray?

Prince: Religion, huh.
Prince: Never really thought much about that.
Prince: Ain’t nobody taught me what it means.

Prince: But you know what?
Prince: Advice is advice.
Prince: If an old man with kind eyes tells you to go find someone
Prince: You go.

Prince: Can’t be worse than what I been doin’.
Prince: Can’t be darker than what I already seen.

Prince: So yeah…
Prince: I think I’ll go.
Prince: Find that Munir guy.

Prince: Maybe he knows somethin’ I don’t.
Prince: Maybe he can tell me what the hell I’m supposed to do with the time I got left.
===
